<title>USA: LOS ANGELES COUNTY ASSESSMENT ROLL JUMPS $3.8 BLN.</title>
<headline>LOS ANGELES COUNTY ASSESSMENT ROLL JUMPS $3.8 BLN.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Los Angeles County reported on Wednesday a $3.8 billion increase in its 1997-1998 assessment roll, reflecting southern California's much improved real estate market.</p>
<p>The increase marked a sharp reversal from the assessment roll declines experienced by the county over each of the last two years, when rolls declined by a total of $12.8 billion, county Assessor Kenneth Hahn said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe we have rounded the bend toward a healthier and more robust real estate market,&quot; Hahn said.</p>
</text>
